From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:29:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: undo the depth layout when the CPU maps
 depth

Depth reaches memory through the color path: within each 80-pixel EDRAM
tile the 40-pixel halves are swapped, and each word is Mesa's Z24S8
byte-swapped and rotated by 8. Undo both in the CPU (de)tiling of
depth/stencil resources. Readback is now exact when the width is a
multiple of 80; in a partial last tile the swapped half falls outside the
resolve and stays wrong (extending the resolve hung the GPU at some sizes;
open).

